          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105164",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-4{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-14 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} &=6 \\\\ {x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{1}=3$, which we substitute into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =-14 \\\\ -4(3)+{x}_{2} & =-14 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=-2$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & =-5 \\\\ 3+4(-2) & =-5 \\\\ -5 & =-5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=-2,$ which means\n\n$$\n3{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-2)=1.\n$$"
